{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>לוא.</b> The alef in the word לו is added, like the alef in הלכוא אתו (Joshua 10:24)." "And note that the vav in ויהי is like a soft peh in the language of Ishmael." "And the meaning: like a river that does not cease, and likewise the waves of the sea."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "The Hebrew lemma לוא appears in the Masoretic text of Isaiah 48:18 with a vav; Ibn Ezra is addressing the alef in the word לו, citing the analogous added alef in the Joshua verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:36.656930720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}